1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:06,531
This healthy offer reserves one hundred simulated USDC against one hundred fifty

2
00:00:06,531 --> 00:00:10,679
collateral units. A trusted issuer controls this local demo.

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:18,908
Valuer publishes a manual zero point sixty-two mark. Loan-to-value reaches one hundred

4
00:00:18,908 --> 00:00:22,847
seven point five percent, so acceptance must fail.

5
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:30,906
The Borrower tab disables Accept offer because the current loan-to-value is above

6
00:00:30,906 --> 00:00:31,314
threshold.

7
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:40,392
Actual direct command returns HTTP four hundred; the loan-to-value guard rejects acceptance.

8
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:49,904
Rejection is atomic. Before and after, contract IDs are unchanged: no loan,

9
00:00:49,904 --> 00:00:55,808
no new principal, and fifty-unit reserve remains. Offer and collateral stay available;

10
00:00:55,808 --> 00:00:57,776
failed command changed nothing.
